{"skill":{"slug":"mixpost","displayName":"Mixpost"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770135797706,"changelog":"Initial release of the Mixpost skill.\n\n- Provides integration with Mixpost, a self-hosted social media management platform.\n- Supports managing accounts, media, tags, and posts using documented API endpoints.\n- Includes setup instructions for environment variables and API authentication.\n- Offers detailed curl examples for common operations: scheduling posts, uploading media, managing tags, and more.\n- Enables management of content across multiple social media platforms from a single interface.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":10206,"sha256":"ba60ee5a49a4e8e50f056cdb05a62584500099d8ca2a668e97e97a9bfab1eed9","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2147,"sha256":"9a102a1ca3bbdd1b72a4b8f5d81f32ec47345a2e2d5c8e931b6c60d048e99895","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789031149086,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"dc133cbeaf92049cd10bb998c8a60927af691ba0a134dca0019999f07a2955c0","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/dc133cbeaf92049cd10bb998c8a60927af691ba0a134dca0019999f07a2955c0","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: mixpost\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides instructions and `curl` examples for interacting with the Mixpost API. All API calls are directed to the user-configured `$MIXPOST_URL` and use provided environment variables (`MIXPOST_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `MIXPOST_WORKSPACE_UUID`) for authentication. While the skill includes a capability to upload local files (e.g., `file=@/path/to/your/file.png`), this is explicitly for uploading media to the Mixpost service, which aligns with its stated purpose. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts against the agent within the `SKILL.md` content.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161130521},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":36,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789031149086},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a straightforward Mixpost API reference that uses a user-provided Mixpost token to manage social media content, with no hidden code or persistence.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Requiring MIXPOST_URL, MIXPOST_ACCESS_TOKEN, and MIXPOST_WORKSPACE_UUID is proportionate for a Mixpost integration, though the token may allow high-impact content changes depending on the user's Mixpost permissions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill with metadata declaring required environment variables; it contains no installer, scripts, dependencies, hooks, or executable payloads.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are scoped to Mixpost API calls, but delete examples include actions that can remove posts from connected social platforms and would benefit from an explicit warning.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, background execution, privilege escalation, local credential harvesting, or system modification behavior is present.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The documented capabilities match the stated Mixpost purpose: listing accounts/media/tags/posts and creating, updating, scheduling, approving, queuing, uploading, and deleting content.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to let the agent operate your Mixpost workspace. Use the least-privileged Mixpost token available, confirm the configured MIXPOST_URL is your own instance, and review any create, publish, approve, schedule, or delete action before it is run.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The artifact tells the user how to create and set a Mixpost access token in environment variables; it does not read local credential files or attempt credential theft.\n[E1] expected: The ping and read examples send authenticated requests to the user's configured MIXPOST_URL, which is necessary for a Mixpost API skill.\n[E1] expected: The update examples transmit post data to the user's configured Mixpost instance, which is purpose-aligned for managing social media posts.\n[SQP-2] expected: Delete examples are part of normal content management, but users should verify targets and delete_mode because some modes can affect connected social accounts.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031149086}}}}}